# Day 31

**26km  / 7 hours**

It's been a month since I started! Have come ~730km in that time so that's cool. I have more resolve to continue now than when I started. 

The day began nicely enough although I didn't sleep very well due to being in a tent near the highway and cars or trucks were blasting along with typical volume. It was quite warm in the morning though which was a sign of things to come. The track began with a short road walk to a boggy track which fed through to a track that weaved under some bridges before aligning itself with the highway on one side and the Waikato River on the other. 

![The river with the road on the right](./river-early.jpg)

After that it was a fairly dull track for a while until it peeled away from the road but started close to the river and there was some actually interesting walking. Signs showed the care and thought going into the area's maintenance and upkeep although the sign showing the lush beautiful forests that once would've inhabited before the bush was all destroyed for farmland was a little depressing. Especially since it was hot at this point and proper tree cover to regulate temperatures would have been appreciated. 

![A goat chilling under cover watching me waltz by](./goat.jpg)

After that relatively nice section it reverted back to some not so appealing road/farm walk for a while until getting to the town at the end of the day. Can't win them all. 
